---
title: Razorbill
---
# Razorbill

The razorbill is a black-and-white auk of the north Atlantic with a deep,
blunt bill crossed by a white line. It pursues sandeels and sprats well below
the surface, driven by half-folded wings, and will work a hundred metres down
when the shoals are deep. The single egg is sharply pointed at one end and is
laid on a bare ledge or in a crevice, where its shape makes it roll in a tight
arc rather than off the rock. Colonies disperse to the open ocean outside the
breeding season. See [[alcidae]].
